sbx plan — preview of the persistent sandbox for this worktree

project:          app
worktree root:    /src/app/wt1
common git dir:   /src/app/.git
sandbox identity: app-wt1-cd4c9147
volume namespace: 53ee4efe (project volumes are named 53ee4efe-<logical name>)

configuration (sbx.toml):
  image:   alpine:3.20
  cpus:    2
  memory:  2G
  shell:   /bin/sh

sandbox:
  workspace: /workspace (the worktree root, read-write, also the working directory)
  mounts:
    - tmpfs /tmp (512M)
  volumes:
    - cache: project volume 53ee4efe-cache at /var/cache
    (compatibility with existing volumes is checked before any creation)
  environment:
    - MODE=test
  network: policy allowlist, deny by default, TLS interception on, dns 1.1.1.1
  secrets (values never appear in this plan):
    - TOKEN: host variable SBX_PLAN_TOKEN, sent only to example.com
  secret map passed as --secret-conf:
    TOKEN:
      value: "${SBX_PLAN_TOKEN}"
      allow: [example.com]

msb arguments at creation:
  msb create --name app-wt1-cd4c9147 alpine:3.20 --cpus 2 --memory 2G --mount-dir /src/app/wt1:/workspace --mount-named 53ee4efe-cache:/var/cache --env MODE=test --label sbx.managed=1 --label sbx.mode=persistent --label sbx.worktree=/src/app/wt1 --net-rule allow@example.com --tls-intercept --dns-nameserver 1.1.1.1 --secret-conf "<secret map generated at creation>" --fs-conf "<filesystem configuration generated at creation>"

sbx changed nothing: no sandbox was created and no host or project
state was written.
